    sh:description "Benchmark Specification, is a versioned specification of one benchmark used in performance comparison, covering return kind (total return, price, excess return), currency, tax treatment, rebalance, availability, and its relation to an instrument, used for unifying the benchmark references that were previously scattered and inconsistent, and for allowing a documented no-suitable-benchmark case with a reason.";
